cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "llmlang (LLL)"
message: "If you use llmlang in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stadelmann
    given-names: Didier
repository-code: "https://github.com/didier1969/llmlang"
abstract: >-
  llmlang is a purely functional, statically verified, compiled programming
  language designed for LLM coding agents rather than for human ergonomics
  first. Contracts (requires/ensures) and termination are discharged at compile
  time by the Z3 SMT solver: an undischarged proof obligation is a compile error
  carrying a counter-model, never a runtime check. Identity is the Blake3 hash of
  the alpha-normalized AST, so renaming is mechanical and hash-preserving.
  Integers are arbitrary-precision with a checked i64 fast path, and the compiler
  emits Rust.
keywords:
  - programming-language
  - formal-verification
  - smt-solver
  - z3
  - design-by-contract
  - functional-programming
  - compiler
  - llm
  - code-generation
license: Apache-2.0
